@ [seal_formation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Candidate_Seal_And_Independent_Review.sop

& [ReviewIdentity] is exact
  + [review_uuid] is fe8aa664-3f31-4a02-9b62-0639f278b90d
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [baseline_commit] is 99d4e81582b8d0afc5f329a83b480955f8292ef1
  + [status] is checkpoint_complete_pure_vocabulary_revision_selected

& [ClosedSupport] is exact
  + one complete supplied inventory is structurally closed, canonically encoded, and digest committed
  + two complete digest carriers can be independently rederived and compared only after exact profile, limits, and root identity scope passes
  + Equal means only equal canonical supplied sequence commitments under the declared scope
  + Different remains an ordinary comparable relation
  + complete positional lineage is retained without acquisition-order meaning
  + 395 tests in debug and overflow-checked release, quality gates, audit, and recursive evidence pass
  + physical origin, acquisition ordering, repeated observation, quiescence, receipt, admission, and every effect remain absent

& [CrossAuthorityConflict] is material before M2C
  + Phase3 Strict Pure Machine Forms defines ConsistencyClass as quiescent_double_inventory or os_snapshot_proven
  + TopologyReceipt 0.2 permits only quiescent_double_inventory
  + the topology scanner formation says a repeated complete inventory yields quiescent_double_inventory
  + the digest reconciliation authority correctly reserves quiescent_double_inventory for a later lifecycle with process and writer accounting
  + equal first and second inventories cannot exclude a transient change-and-restore between observations
  + equal first and second inventories cannot exclude a change immediately after the second observation
  + supervisor-owned process quiescence cannot exclude every external writer without a separately proven enforcement primitive
  + therefore the existing label risks converting an observation method into an unsupported world-state claim

& [FaultClassification] is semantic authority inflation
  + [not_a_code_fault] no producer, receipt issuer, persistent receipt, or external consumer exists
  + [not_a_reconciliation_fault] the new module deliberately refuses temporal and quiescence meaning
  + [formation_fault] prior formation repaired atomic-snapshot overclaim but retained a label that still overstates the weakest evidence
  + [containment] M2C, M2D, receipt issuance, mutation, seal, and every physical effect remain locked
  + [repair_window] is now, before any physical producer can emit the old vocabulary

& [EvidenceLattice] separates observation from state
  + [supplied_pair_equal] is pure equality of two caller-supplied canonical sequence commitments with no physical or temporal grade
  + [non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal] requires two actual complete acquisitions under one exact scope, an independently evidenced first-then-second order, and equal commitments
  + [supervisor_quiesced_repeated_inventory_equal] would additionally require exact owned-process shutdown and supervisor write exclusion but still preserve external-writer uncertainty
  + [os_snapshot_proven] requires a separately proven platform snapshot primitive and exact snapshot identity
  + no weaker grade implies a stronger grade
  + this slice selects only non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal and preserves os_snapshot_proven as a separately gated stronger vocabulary
  + supervisor_quiesced_repeated_inventory_equal is deferred until its lifecycle evidence and enforcement boundary are designed

& [CandidateComparison] is dependency ordered
  + [candidate_A] proceed directly to M2C physical scanner implementation
    - rejected because the current output vocabulary would force a producer either to overclaim quiescence or to emit no valid receipt
  + [candidate_B] construct TopologyReceipt from the pure reconciliation result
    - rejected because physical origin, acquisition order, complete enumeration, policy binding, predecessor binding, nonce, time, issuer, and receipt authority are absent
  + [candidate_C] rename Equal to stable or unchanged
    - rejected because it launders temporal meaning into a pure supplied comparison
  + [candidate_D] keep quiescent_double_inventory but add a documentation disclaimer
    - rejected because the serialized enum itself is public machine meaning and cannot be repaired by prose contrary to its name
  + [candidate_E] add every conceivable evidence-strength variant now
    - rejected as speculative growth without a producer, consumer, or proof route
  + [candidate_F] perform one narrow pure consistency-evidence vocabulary revision
    + replace ConsistencyClass with InventoryConsistencyEvidence where used by the topology receipt path
    + replace quiescent_double_inventory with non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
    + rename the receipt field from consistency to consistency_evidence so it denotes proof grade rather than an asserted state
    + retain os_snapshot_proven but forbid production until its primitive and provenance are separately authorized
    + strictly reject the legacy field and old enum string rather than silently migrate
    + revise Phase3 and topology form profiles because serialized machine meaning changes
    + update formation documents by lineage rather than rewriting preserved historical source
    + implement only safe pure serde forms, validation, tests, evidence, and closure after full SJS

& [SelectedBoundary] is Phase3 inventory consistency evidence vocabulary revision
  + [profile_candidate] is cantor-phase3-inventory-consistency-evidence-revision/0.1
  + [phase3_forms_profile_candidate] is cantor-phase3-machine-forms/0.2
  + [topology_forms_profile_candidate] is cantor-phase3-topology-forms/0.3
  + [topology_receipt_profile_candidate] is cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.3
  + [scanner_profile] remains cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1 because no scanner behavior is implemented
  + [target_modules] are existing crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/phase3_evidence.rs and topology_forms.rs only after signed authority
  + [dependency_delta] is zero
  + [effect_delta] is zero

& [SelectedMeaning] is minimal and inspectable
  + [InventoryConsistencyEvidence.NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual] means the authorized issuer claims two actual complete ordered acquisitions under exact common scope and equal canonical commitments
  + [NonAtomic] denies snapshot, transaction, lock, or uninterrupted-state meaning
  + [RepeatedInventory] requires two actual physical inventory acquisitions rather than two supplied values
  + [Equal] concerns their committed canonical subjects only
  + [InventoryConsistencyEvidence.OsSnapshotProven] remains a closed reserved stronger value requiring separately bound platform proof
  + [TopologyReceipt.consistency_evidence] stores the evidence grade and never names the candidate state simply consistent

& [RequiredProvenance] prevents pure-form self-authorization
  + validity of the enum and receipt form proves syntax and relation coherence only
  + a future M2C producer must bind distinct acquisition identities, first and second acquisition ordering, exact common scope, both complete carrier lineages, and reconciliation result
  + a future receipt issuer must bind candidate root, root identity, root volume-GUID path, predecessor admission, policy, scanner profile, nonce, counts, totals, issued and expiry ticks, and the evidence lineage
  + this revision does not itself add those producer records or issue a receipt

& [CompatibilityDecision] is strict rejection
  + no live scanner, receipt issuer, persisted topology receipt, mutation consumer, or external API depends on the old serialized value
  + old quiescent_double_inventory input is rejected
  + old consistency field input is rejected
  + old Phase3 forms 0.1, topology forms 0.2, and receipt 0.2 profiles are rejected by revised decoders
  + preserved historical evidence remains historical and is never rewritten to claim the new grade

& [RequirementDelta] is proposed P3ICER-001 through P3ICER-014
  + exact multi-source preservation and supersession
  + evidence-versus-state delineation
  + new closed enum and renamed receipt field
  + strict legacy rejection
  + profile revisions and unchanged scanner profile
  + topology receipt invariant preservation
  + pure safe implementation and dependency neutrality
  + focused, global, audit, recursive, provenance, rollback, and nonclaim proof
  + [authority_state] raw_source_not_yet_preserved

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  - no filesystem, Windows call, handle, pointer, unsafe, process, environment, clock, random, network, persistence, database, Git runtime, model, tool, physical acquisition, fixture, receipt issuance, admission, mutation, seal, test execution, cleanup, or promotion
  - no conversion from supplied Equal to repeated physical evidence
  - no claim that repeated equality proves no intermediate, subsequent, or external change
  - no source rewriting; revisions preserve and supersede prior source and canonical artifacts
  - stop on hidden legacy acceptance, unchanged profile with changed JSON, speculative evidence variants, dependency growth, effect surface, or failed proof

& [Decision] is source preservation and full SJS before code
  + [next] preserve one verbose raw revision source plus exact manifest
  + [then] run input audit, delineation, explosion, semantic refinement, constraint reapplication, pruning and growth, seven-fold exhaustion, data design, justification, plan, registry, matrix, slice, phase lock, canonical revision, and replacement satisfaction signature
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [physical_authority] is absent
